        247.98619079589844,
        297.2486877441406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "0.860 ± 0.031",
      "bbox": [
        272.8575439453125,
        288.30224609375,
        325.01959228515625,
        303.9653015136719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "21.0 ± 1.27",
      "bbox": [
        335.85284423828125,
        288.30224609375,
        378.9962158203125,
        303.9653015136719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Soft (0.9)",
      "bbox": [
        213.38299560546875,
        300.01104736328125,
        247.98619079589844,
        308.0818176269531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "0.814 ± 0.105",
      "bbox": [
        272.8575439453125,
        299.1353759765625,
        325.01959228515625,
        314.7984313964844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "20.5 ± 1.78",
      "bbox": [
        335.85284423828125,
        299.1353759765625,
        378.9962158203125,
        314.7984313964844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "with resampling, and compare resamplers while holding the rest of the system fixed. Resampling itself can interact with",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        335.787353515625,
        541.44091796875,
        344.69390869140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the optimisation process in non-trivial ways, and we thus primarily evaluate the comparison by end-to-end performance.",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        347.74237060546875,
        543.1786499023438,
        356.64892578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "However, tempering the observation likelihood in the first setting reduces weight concentration: the weights become more",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        359.6983642578125,
        541.4353637695312,
        368.60491943359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "uniform and ESS remains high. With this ESS-based adaptive resampling, the resampling can therefore be triggered",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        371.6533508300781,
        541.4410400390625,
        380.5599060058594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "infrequently. As such, to further stress test differentiable resampling in this context, we consider the second setting with",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        383.6083679199219,
        541.44091796875,
        392.5149230957031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "more concentrated weights and resampling at nearly every filtering step.",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        395.5633544921875,
        342.7912292480469,
        404.46990966796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "As we have seen, even in this challenging setting, diffusion resampling remains competitive among the baselines. Figure 10",
      "bbox": [
        55.082000732421875,
        413.4963684082031,
        541.44482421875,
        422.4029235839844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "shows a qualitative comparison of a top performing model in each resampling class in this setting. Here, the diffusion",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        425.45135498046875,
        541.44091796875,
        434.35791015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "resampler is among the three top-performing baselines. While soft resampling occasionally shows better performance in",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        437.4063720703125,
        541.43505859375,
        446.31292724609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "terms of final metrics compared to diffusion resampling, see Figure 9, we note that it also exhibits significantly worse",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        449.3613586425781,
        541.4407348632812,
        458.2679138183594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "weight degeneracy compared to diffusion resampling and the other baselines. In addition, it is by construction not fully",
      "bbox": [
        55.082000732421875,
        461.3173522949219,
        541.7842407226562,
        470.2239074707031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "differentiable (see Table 20). We also note that while OT produces the top performing model here, it exhibits high variability",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        473.2723693847656,
        541.791748046875,
        482.1789245605469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and is overall unstable in this setting, with only a few converging training runs.",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        485.22735595703125,
        369.8993835449219,
        494.1339111328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Identifiability of the latent space",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        510.88580322265625,
        194.35794067382812,
        519.8421630859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Because both the transition model fθ and the decoder rϕ are learnt only through the",
      "bbox": [
        204.31886291503906,
        510.8459777832031,
        541.4390869140625,
        521.4069213867188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "image observation likelihood, the latent state is typically identifiable only up to (possibly nonlinear) invertible transforma-",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        522.9613647460938,
        543.0967407226562,
        531.867919921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tions, and there is no unique correspondence between the learnt states and the true physical coordinates without special",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        534.9163818359375,
        541.4409790039062,
        543.8229370117188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "constructions (see, e.g., Greydanus et al., 2019, for a similar issue). For this reason, we do not directly evaluate the pendulum",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        546.871337890625,
        541.4400024414062,
        555.7778930664062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "dynamics in state space, but instead assess model quality in the observation space via image reconstruction metrics. A similar",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        558.8263549804688,
        541.6060791015625,
        567.73291015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "evaluation strategy is common in recent work on latent SDEs for high-dimensional sequence data. For example, both Bartosh",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        570.7813720703125,
        541.4400024414062,
        579.6879272460938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "et al. (2025) and Course & Nair (2023) primarily report qualitative comparisons of generated image sequences in comparable",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        582.736328125,
        541.4400634765625,
        591.6428833007812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "settings, rather than quantitative metrics in the latent state space, reflecting the view that high-quality reconstruction is",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        594.6923828125,
        541.4408569335938,
        603.5989379882812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "indicative of a meaningful latent representation. Nevertheless, we find that sometimes the learnt dynamics closely match the",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        606.6473388671875,
        541.4375,
        615.5538940429688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "true pendulum dynamics up to a linear transformation of the latent coordinates. Figure 11 illustrates two such examples with",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        618.6023559570312,
        541.440185546875,
        627.5089111328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the latent dynamics learnt using diffusion resampling, where a simple linear transformation of the latent trajectory yields",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        630.557373046875,
        541.435791015625,
        639.4639282226562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "a close match to the ground-truth pendulum state (coefficient of determination R2 ≈0.98 (left) and R2 ≈0.92 (right),",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        637.9309692382812,
        542.6860961914062,
        658.8310546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "respectively). This indicates that the models have learnt meaningful latent representations of the underlying pendulum",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        654.4673461914062,
        541.44091796875,
        663.3739013671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "dynamics, albeit in a transformed coordinate system.",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        666.42333984375,
        265.7305603027344,
        675.3298950195312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Network architectures",
      "bbox": [
